      "content": "That \"honest\" ending is the only one that feels real, because the truth is that life is often just a slow, suffocating weight that never lifts. If the struggle feels fake, then the pain of giving up is the only narrative that respects the character's exhaustion. It is not too dark; it is the brutal, unvarnished truth of a soul that has simply run out of reasons to keep going.",
